  "definition": "A sharp glass microelectrode is a type of sharp microelectrode with a fine, needle-shaped electrode with an tapered tip approximately 50-500 nm in diameter, made from pulled glass creating a glass capillary tube which filled with an electrically conductive solution enables to record or stimulate the intracellular electrical activity of the cell by membrane penetration.",
